{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "03339",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.16,
      "end_seconds": 2.81,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "Welcome. Make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 3.96,
      "end_seconds": 5.12,
      "duration_seconds": 1.16,
      "text": "hello, doctor"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 6.83,
      "end_seconds": 13.35,
      "duration_seconds": 6.52,
      "text": "doctor, I've come along because I know the history, if it helps"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.36,
      "end_seconds": 20.94,
      "duration_seconds": 5.58,
      "text": "good, that'll be useful. Pull up a chair. You came on your own today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 21.71,
      "end_seconds": 24.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Yes, I managed on my own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.66,
      "end_seconds": 28.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Start wherever you like, I'm listening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 31.92,
      "end_seconds": 35.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "We came because of shivering that has stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.97,
      "end_seconds": 39.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.49,
      "text": "Let me quickly check your readings."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.49,
      "end_seconds": 48.01,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "keep your arm relaxed for me.."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.79,
      "end_seconds": 70.33,
      "duration_seconds": 9.54,
      "text": "Okay: pulse is 82 beats a minute, saturation 99 percent, temp 36.6 degrees. And BP is 119 over 77."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 81.46,
      "end_seconds": 84.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "has this been going on for long?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 85.03,
      "end_seconds": 87.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "I'd say three days, maybe."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 88.85,
      "end_seconds": 92.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "It was closer to five days, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 96.62,
      "end_seconds": 101.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "okay, so roughly three to five days. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.92,
      "end_seconds": 108.21,
      "duration_seconds": 5.29,
      "text": "Sorry, what was I saying, yes, somewhere around that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.64,
      "end_seconds": 112.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "how much does it limit you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.24,
      "end_seconds": 118.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "I'd give it a four, out of ten"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.9,
      "end_seconds": 122.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Is it accompanied by anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.75,
      "end_seconds": 141.14,
      "duration_seconds": 13.39,
      "text": "It usually comes with being found cold and drowsy. I've also had confusion. With confusion, it feels moderate to me. About being found cold and drowsy, moderate, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 142.6,
      "end_seconds": 148.55,
      "duration_seconds": 5.95,
      "text": "have you had shivering that has stopped before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.6,
      "end_seconds": 160.36,
      "duration_seconds": 6.76,
      "text": "Yes, something like this happened last year, and it went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 169.24,
      "end_seconds": 173.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.46,
      "text": "So, any head injury, fall or alcohol at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.09,
      "end_seconds": 178.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "No, nothing to report there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 182.49,
      "end_seconds": 185.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "How are your bowels, any trouble?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.37,
      "end_seconds": 188.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "no, that side's been fine"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.85,
      "end_seconds": 192.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "anything unusual with passing urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.44,
      "end_seconds": 196.09,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "Nothing there, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.5,
      "end_seconds": 201.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "alright, what does a normal day of food look like?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 202.76,
      "end_seconds": 206.15,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Lots of rice, lentils and some fruit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 206.95,
      "end_seconds": 209.14,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "Alright, how active are you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 210.47,
      "end_seconds": 213.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "I hardly move around during the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.49,
      "end_seconds": 216.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "And your job?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 217.77,
      "end_seconds": 221.27,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "I work in accounts at a hospital"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 223.23,
      "end_seconds": 227.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Has anyone in your family had anything serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 227.88,
      "end_seconds": 230.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.09,
      "text": "My daughter has type 1 diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.66,
      "end_seconds": 235.58,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 236.32,
      "end_seconds": 241.94,
      "duration_seconds": 5.62,
      "text": "Escitalopram i take it 10 milligrams, maybe, once a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.69,
      "end_seconds": 246.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.19,
      "text": "Is the packet here, or the prescription?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 251.16,
      "end_seconds": 253.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Oh, no, it's at home."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.21,
      "end_seconds": 258.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Any health conditions I should have on record?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 260.82,
      "end_seconds": 269.08,
      "duration_seconds": 8.26,
      "text": "I've had depression for about a year now. I've had anxiety for five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.72,
      "end_seconds": 278.8,
      "duration_seconds": 9.08,
      "text": "I follow. Right, yes, anxiety is known to us, good to have that clear. Have you had any surgical procedures?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 279.75,
      "end_seconds": 286.06,
      "duration_seconds": 6.31,
      "text": "just a a mole taken off my arm, a few years ago"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.68,
      "end_seconds": 292.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "right, let's have a a proper look at you"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 293.65,
      "end_seconds": 294.56,
      "duration_seconds": 0.91,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 295.47,
      "end_seconds": 298.7,
      "duration_seconds": 3.23,
      "text": "stay as you are for a moment"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 313.96,
      "end_seconds": 321.29,
      "duration_seconds": 7.33,
      "text": "your temperature is twenty-nine degrees, your skin is ice cold and your pulse is very slow"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 326.68,
      "end_seconds": 328.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "All finished, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 344.56,
      "end_seconds": 374.53,
      "duration_seconds": 29.97,
      "text": "So where does that leave us? It points towards severe hypothermia. I'm going to order an ECG, for bradycardia. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more. I'm going to order blood tests, for hypothermia. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture. We should do a blood sugar for hypothermia. Handle gently and warm slowly with warm blankets and warm fluids through the drip."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 375.84,
      "end_seconds": 379.67,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "I think the emergency team should see you too"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 380.5,
      "end_seconds": 382.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Sure, where do I go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 383.88,
      "end_seconds": 404.19,
      "duration_seconds": 20.31,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose. The thing that would worry me is if the symptoms get worse. If that happens, go to emergency. I'd like to see you again straight away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 405.39,
      "end_seconds": 409.96,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "I, I'll book it on my way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 411.26,
      "end_seconds": 415.82,
      "duration_seconds": 4.56,
      "text": "is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 417.8,
      "end_seconds": 419.48,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "That's clear, thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 421.22,
      "end_seconds": 422.43,
      "duration_seconds": 1.21,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}